    body = [=[
\**{c=red:Note:}** This Mission is essentially identical for all 3 {z:Nations}. While each {z:Nations} requires you to travel to the other two, they all follow the same path.
:* {p:San d'Orians|San d'Oria} and {p:Windurstians|Windurst} who choose {p:Bastok} first will do the same things. Therefore, it IS possible to group people together from different {z:Nations} to ultimately end up on the same BCNM fight.
:* A {p:Windurstian|Windurst} may choose to do the {p:Bastok} portion first, and {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion second, while a {p:Bastokan|Bastok} can do the {p:Windurstian|Windurst} portion first, and the {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion second. In this scenario, {p:Windurstians|Windurst} and {p:Bastokans|Bastok} can enter the same BCNM for the {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion.
:* Players who have already completed this Mission (for any {z:Nation}) may enter any of the BC, except for the one associated with their Nation (A {p:Windurstian|Windurst} who has completed 2-3 is unable to enter the Giddeus BCNM to help others, unless they have completed this battle through another Nation's 2-3 Mission).

=2 Walkthrough
Trade three {p:Crystals} (3+ if you skipped the previous mission) to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the {n:Gate Guard}.
* This Mission can be long if you do not have {p:Home Points|Home Point}, and is broken down in to two legs. Whichever Nation you choose first determines how the next plays out. Option 2, the {p:San d'Oria} path progression, is typically easier and faster.
* Speak with {n:Kupipi} in {z:Heavens Tower}. She is inside the **Clerical Chamber**. She will give you a {@k} {p:Letter to the consuls}.
** You may receive {i:Cipher: Semih|Cipher: Semih|10157} if you don't already have it and are participating in {p:Trust}.

=2 Option 1: Bastok Path
=3 Windurst to Bastok
* Speak to {n:Patt-Pott} in {p:Bastok} {z:Metalworks} {p:HP#1|HP}. He is inside the **Windurstian Consulate** top floor (I-7).
* Speak to {n:Pius} in the **President's Office Department of Industry** (J-8).
* Speak to {n:Grohm} at (H-9) in the **Craftsmen's Eatery**. He will give you 3 {@i:Pickaxe|605} {i:Pickaxes|Pickaxe|605}. Consider buying more, as they can break.
* Make your way to {z:Palborough Mines} in {z:North Gustaberg}, at the very north of the zone. You will need to mine {@i:Mine Gravel|597} {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} from the **Mythril Seams** located throughout the zone. There is one on the first floor at (I-8) on the west side of the river, and one on the top floor at (I-9). Trade the {i:Pickaxe|Pickaxe|605} to the **Seam** until you receive some {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597}. Note: the seams are different from mining points. They will not be visually indicated on the map. Mining points do not yield Mine Gravel.
** You CAN purchase {@i:Mine Gravel|597} {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} from the {z:Auction House}. ({@g:Auction House} > Others > Misc. 1)
** If you care about the {p:"Mythril Marathon" 15th Vana'versary RoE Objective|Category:Records of Eminence} ultimately used for the {i:Omega Mount}, set that objective before you do the next step - it requires 10 {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} turned into {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599}.
* Once you receive the {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597}, head to the second floor, and make your way to (I-7). Trade the gravel to the refiner and then pull the lever. Drop off the ledge to the level below and pull another lever. You will receive {@i:Mythril Sand|599} {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599}.
* Trade the {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599} to {n:Patt-Pott}. Talk to him once more. This is the end of the {p:Bastok} leg.

=3 Bastok to San d'Oria
* Speak to {n:Kasaroro} in the Windurstian Consulate in {z:Northern San d'Oria} (H-9).
* Speak to {p:Halver} in {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}.
** You will receive {i:Cipher: Halver|Cipher: Halver|10158} if you don't already have it. If not received, it may be received later.
* Go to {z:Horlais Peak} and clear the BCNM "The Rank 2 Final Mission".
** If you are low level consider forming a party (and/or use {p:Trusts|Trust}) of level 25 or higher, but make sure everyone has gear for a level 25 fight. A {p:BLM} or {p:RDM} is ideal for this fight, as you'll want sleep.
** To get to {z:Horlais Peak} use the Homepoint to {z:Yughott Grotto} or make your way to {z:Ghelsba Outpost} from {z:West Ronfaure}, it is in the northwestern corner. Inside, follow the left wall until you zone in to {z:Yughott Grotto}. Follow it all the way to the end, around (K-5). You should exit to {z:Fort Ghelsba}.
** Outside, head straight and stick to the left wall. You should start going up hill. Follow it around. At the top, there will be a large hut to your right. Enter it and go to the back, there is a hidden entrance here. It returns to {z:Yughott Grotto}#4. Head for (J-6) to enter {z:Horlais Peak}.
** Prepare and enter. Buffs will wear on zone, so buff up inside. Make your way to the top to face off against two NMs, an {p:Ahriman|Category:Ahriman} called {m:Seeker} and a {p:Dragon|Category:Dragon} called {m:Dread Dragon}.
** Sleep the Dragon and then defeat the Seeker, who is weak. Attack the dragon and take it down. This fight is really easy with a full party.
** If you are low level it can easily be defeated with a {p:MNK}/{p:WAR} and {p:WHM}/{p:BLM}. Can be soloed by some jobs with a lot of meds, and duoed by almost any melee job with a {p:WHM} healer.
* Return to {n:Kasaroro} at {z:Northern San d'Oria} after clearing the BCNM.
* Return to {n:Kupipi} in {z:Heavens Tower} to complete the Mission.

=2 Option 2: San d'Oria Path
=3 Windurst to San d'Oria
* Make your way to {p:San d'Oria} and visit the **Windurstian Consulate** in {z:Northern San d'Oria}.
* Speak to {n:Heruze-Moruze} and then {n:Kasaroro}, both at (H-9).
* Head over to {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} and speak to {p:Halver}.
** This NPC is involved in multiple different Quests and Missions, you may need to speak to him repeatedly until he sends you to {z:Ghelsba Outpost}.
** {z:Ghelsba Outpost} is located to the far northwestern corner of {z:West Ronfaure}.
* Inside, head for (H-7) and look for the NM {m:Warchief Vatgit} and defeat him (its only purpose is for this Mission, and is usually up and wandering around. If not, wait a short time, it doesn't take long).
** The {p:Survival Guide} to {z:Fort Ghelsba} will bring you close to the NM. Just zone back out to Ghelsba and across the bridge.
* Speak to {n:Kasaroro} again. You are now finished with the {p:San d'Oria} half of this Mission.

=3 San d'Oria to Bastok
* Make your way to {p:Bastok}. Enter the {z:Metalworks} from {z:Bastok Markets}. Make your way to the top and speak with {n:Patt-Pott} inside the **Windurstian Consulate**, around (I-7).
* Speak to {n:Pius} in the **President's Office Department of Industry** (J-8). He will send you to the **Craftsmen's Eatery** (H-9) to speak to {n:Grohm}.
** If you're low level, form a party (and/or use {p:Trusts|Trust}) of level 25 or higher, but make sure everyone has gear for a level 25 fight. A {p:BLM} or {p:RDM} is ideal for this fight, as you'll want sleep.
* Make your way to {z:Palborough Mines}, in the very far north of {z:North Gustaberg}.
** If you've already been there, take {z:Palborough Mines} {p:Home Point #1|Home Point}.
* Inside, make your way to (I-8) and head upstairs. Here, make your way to (H-10) and zone in to {z:Waughroon Shrine}.
* Prepare and enter. Buffs will wear on zone, so buff up inside. Make your way to the top to face off against two NMs, an {p:Ahriman|Category:Ahriman} called {m:Seeker} and a {p:Dragon|Category:Dragon} called {m:Dark Dragon}.
** **This fight is trivial with trusts**
** Sleep the Dragon and then defeat the Seeker, who is weak. Attack the dragon and take it down. This fight is really easy with a full party.
** It can easily be defeated with a {p:MNK}/{p:WAR} and {p:WHM}/{p:BLM}. Can be soloed by some jobs with a lot of meds, and duoed by almost any melee job with a {p:WHM} healer.
* Once cleared, return to {n:Patt-Pott} in {z:Metalworks}.
* Your journey is almost complete, head back to {z:Heavens Tower} in {z:Windurst Walls} and speak to {n:Kupipi} to complete the Mission and receive your rewards.

